# Fibonacci using Memoization (Top-Down DP)

## Problem Statement
n-th Fibonacci number , solve evry subproblem.

## Pseudocode
```
memo[0..n] = -1

FIB_MEMO(n):
    if n <= 1: return n
    if memo[n] != -1: return memo[n]
    memo[n] = FIB_MEMO(n - 1) + FIB_MEMO(n - 2)
    return memo[n]
```

## Flowchart
```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A([Start: FIB_MEMO n]) --> B{n <= 1?}
    B -- Yes --> C[Return n] --> Z([End])
    B -- No --> D{memo n already hai?}
    D -- Yes --> E[Return memo n] --> Z
    D -- No --> F[memo n = FIB_MEMO n-1 + FIB_MEMO n-2]
    F --> G[Return memo n] --> Z
```

## Time & Space Complexity
| | Recursive | Memoized |
|---|---|---|
| Time | O(2ⁿ) | **O(n)** |
| Space | O(n) | O(n) (memo table + stack) |

## Recursive vs Memoized (same n pe)
| n | Recursive calls | Memoized calls |
|---|---|---|
| 10 | 177 | 19 |
| 35 | 29,860,703 | 69 |

Memoized me calls hamesha `2n - 1` aate hain.

## Sample Input / Output
```
n = 10  -> fib(10) = 55, Total recursive calls = 19
n = 35  -> fib(35) = 9227465, Total recursive calls = 69
n = 92  -> fib(92) = 7540113804746346429, Total recursive calls = 183
```


